# CT Monitor Service Architecture

## Overview

The CT Monitor Service watches newly issued SSL/TLS certificates for two independent per-program features: **typosquat detection** (`ct_monitoring_enabled` — protected-domain matching → NATS alerts) and **asset monitoring** (`ct_asset_monitoring_enabled` — program-scope matching → subdomain ingest via `POST /assets`). It consumes an aggregated certificate stream from **self-hosted [certstream-server](https://github.com/CaliDog/certstream-server)** via [certstream-python](https://github.com/CaliDog/certstream-python).

## Core Architecture

```
certstream-server (kubernetes/base/certstream-server)
    ↓ WebSocket ws://certstream:4000/
CertStreamConsumer (certstream_consumer.py) — certstream-python in a thread + asyncio queue
    ↓ CertificateInfo
CTMonitorService (main.py)
├── DnstwistVariationGenerator — PRIMARY: O(1) variation lookup (typosquat)
├── protected_domain_similarity.py — keywords + API-aligned similarity (typosquat)
├── scope_matcher.py — program scope matching (asset monitoring)
├── CTAlertPublisher — NATS JetStream (typosquat alerts + CT asset discovery events)
└── CTAssetSubmitter (asset_submitter.py) — batched POST /assets (asset monitoring)
```

## Infrastructure

| Component | Path | Notes |
|-----------|------|--------|
| certstream-server | [`kubernetes/base/certstream-server/`](kubernetes/base/certstream-server/) | **0 replicas by default**; ct-monitor scales to **1** when any program has `ct_monitoring_enabled` **or** `ct_asset_monitoring_enabled`, back to **0** when none |
| ct-monitor | [`kubernetes/base/ct-monitor/`](kubernetes/base/ct-monitor/) | `CERTSTREAM_URL` from `service-config`; patches `deployments/scale` via [`certstream_k8s.py`](../../src/ct-monitor/app/certstream_k8s.py) + [`ct-monitor-rbac.yaml`](../../kubernetes/base/ct-monitor/ct-monitor-rbac.yaml) |
| Image | `ghcr.io/.../certstream-server:1.6.0` | **Independent** of reconhawx `APP_VERSION` — see [`third-party/certstream-server/VERSION`](../../third-party/certstream-server/VERSION) |

## Component Responsibilities

### CTMonitorService (`main.py`)
- Orchestrates lifecycle, HTTP control API, stats
- **CertStream ingestion** only when `≥1` program has `ct_monitoring_enabled` **or** `ct_asset_monitoring_enabled` (`_reconcile_ct_ingestion` every 2s)
- **certstream-server replicas** scaled 0/1 in the same reconcile loop (scale up → HTTP ready poll → start consumer; scale down after stop consumer)
- **Pod auto-start**: lifespan probes API then `start()`; set `CT_MONITOR_AUTO_START=false` to idle until `POST /start`
- Program config reload: API `sync_ct_monitor_program_config()` → `POST /refresh-domains` (triggered by CT flag, protected-domain, or **scope** field changes)

### CertStreamConsumer (`certstream_consumer.py`)
- **Primary** ingress: `certstream.listen_for_events` pattern via `CertStreamClient` in a daemon thread
- Bridges messages into asyncio; optional TLD filter at enqueue (off by default — all TLDs matched)
- Reconnects on disconnect (`CT_RECONNECT_DELAY`, default 5s)
- Default URL: `ws://certstream:4000/` (`CERTSTREAM_URL`)

### Configuration sources

| What | Where |
|------|--------|
| CertStream URL | `CERTSTREAM_URL` / ConfigMap `certstream.url` |
| Global stats interval | `system_settings.ct_monitor_runtime`; API internal + admin routes |
| Per-program similarity | `programs.ct_monitor_program_settings.similarity_threshold` on `GET /programs/{name}` |

### DnstwistVariationGenerator / `protected_domain_similarity.py` / `CTAlertPublisher`
- Unchanged: see previous patterns in this file’s matching and alert sections below.

## Data Flow

```
certstream-server (all CT logs)
    ↓
CertStreamConsumer (all TLDs by default; optional CT_INGESTION_TLD_FILTER_ENABLED)
    ↓
CTMonitorService._on_certificate()
    ├─ typosquat: variation match → keyword/similarity → NATS events.typosquat.ct_alert → event-handler
    └─ asset: scope match (scope_matcher) → CTAssetSubmitter → POST /assets → NATS events.assets.ct_subdomain.discovered → event-handler
```

### CT asset monitoring (scope-based subdomain discovery)

- Per-program flag **`programs.ct_asset_monitoring_enabled`** (separate from typosquat's `ct_monitoring_enabled`); UI toggle on the program **Scope** tab ("CT asset discovery").
- [`scope_matcher.py`](../../src/ct-monitor/app/scope_matcher.py) ports the API's `utils/scope_patterns.py` matching (structured `scope_domains`/`out_of_scope_domains` + legacy regex) with **regexes precompiled per config refresh**; keep semantics in sync with the API module.
- `domain_config_builder.build_asset_match_states` builds `ProgramAssetMatchState` (program id + `CompiledScopeMatcher`); an **apex prefilter index** (registrable apex → programs, via `domain_labels.extract_apex_domain`) keeps the per-SAN hot path to one tldextract lookup.
- Asset matching in `match_certificate_sync` runs **before** the typosquat skip rules (`is_legitimate_subdomain` skips exactly what asset monitoring wants); wildcard hostnames are matched/submitted with the leading `*.` stripped. Returns a 4th element: `[(hostname, program_name, program_id), …]`.
- [`asset_submitter.py`](../../src/ct-monitor/app/asset_submitter.py): Redis dedup (`ct_monitor:asset_seen:{program_id}:{hostname}`, `CT_ASSET_CACHE_TTL` default 24h, keys set **only after successful POST**), per-program buffers flushed every `CT_ASSET_FLUSH_INTERVAL` (15s) or at `CT_ASSET_BATCH_MAX` (200) → `POST /assets` `{"program_id", "assets": {"subdomain": [{"name": …}]}}`, then NATS `events.assets.ct_subdomain.discovered` (one event per hostname). **No DNS resolution** — the API inserts subdomains whether or not they resolve and re-checks scope server-side (authoritative).

## Configuration (`config.py`)

**Required:** `API_URL`, `NATS_URL`, `INTERNAL_SERVICE_API_KEY`

**CertStream:** `CERTSTREAM_URL` (default `ws://certstream:4000/`), `CT_RECONNECT_DELAY`

**K8s scaler:** `CT_CERTSTREAM_SCALE_ENABLED` (`true` in cluster; `false` for local dev), `CERTSTREAM_DEPLOYMENT_NAME` (default `certstream-server`), `KUBERNETES_NAMESPACE`, `CT_CERTSTREAM_READY_TIMEOUT` (default 90s). Auto-enables when ServiceAccount token is present unless explicitly off.

**CertStream consumer:** `CERTSTREAM_QUEUE_MAXSIZE` (default 5000), `CERTSTREAM_QUEUE_DROP_WATERMARK` (default 0.8 — drop when queue fill ≥ this ratio).

**Matching throughput:** `CT_MATCH_CONCURRENCY` (default `min(4, cpu_count)` — number of long-lived consumer worker tasks draining the queue; raise with CPU limits on the Deployment).

**Ingestion TLD filter:** `CT_INGESTION_TLD_FILTER_ENABLED` (default `false` — all certificate TLDs). When `true`, uses per-program `tld_filter` union.

**Variations:** unlimited dnstwist permutations per protected domain (no cap unless `max_variations` passed explicitly)

**Asset monitoring:** `CT_ASSET_CACHE_TTL` (default 86400), `CT_ASSET_FLUSH_INTERVAL` (default 15), `CT_ASSET_BATCH_MAX` (default 200)

**Runtime:** `CT_STATS_INTERVAL` (overridable via `ct_monitor_runtime` in DB)

**HTTP:** `CT_MONITOR_HTTP_HOST`, `CT_MONITOR_HTTP_PORT` (default 8002)

## Protected Domains Loading

`GET /programs`, `GET /programs/{name}` for `ct_monitoring_enabled` programs (typosquat config) and `ct_asset_monitoring_enabled` programs (scope matchers from `id` + scope fields); rebuild variations and scope matchers on each reload. Triggers: ct-monitor `start()`, and API `sync_ct_monitor_program_config()` → `POST /refresh-domains` when CT-related program settings change — including scope field edits while asset monitoring is on (no periodic polling).

## Matching Algorithm

Two stages; skip legitimate subdomains of protected FQDNs and exact protected FQDN hits.

**Stage 1 — dnstwist variations (O(1)):** Pre-computed variation **registrable hostname labels** (public suffix stripped via `tldextract` in `domain_labels.hostname_without_public_suffix`). Certificate SANs match when their label equals a variation label **exactly** — any TLD (`d0main.live` matches variation from `d0main.com`; `my-d0main.net` does not).

**Stage 2 — keywords + similarity:** Protected subdomain **keywords** match as substrings of the full hostname (`production` in `production-d0main.live`); one **Aho-Corasick automaton** over all programs' keywords scans each domain once (`build_keyword_automaton` in `domain_config_builder.py`; substring fallback when `pyahocorasick` is unavailable — first program in load order wins either way). Fuzzy match uses **rapidfuzz** Levenshtein (numerically identical to the API's pure-Python scoring; keep logic in sync with API `protected_domain_similarity_service.py`) over precomputed inputs: per-protected `PreparedProtected` (apex/collapsed, built once per config refresh) and per-SAN `PreparedTypo` (suffix fragments + apex/collapsed, built once and shared across programs). Apex extraction via `tldextract` (`domain_labels.py`, bundled PSL snapshot + LRU cache).

### Typosquat alert match / skip matrix

**Program config required:** A program participates in typosquat alerting only when `ct_monitoring_enabled=true` and it has at least one protected input: `protected_domains`, `seed_domains`, `settings.root_domains`, or `protected_subdomain_prefixes`. Protected-domain inputs feed both dnstwist and similarity; prefixes feed keyword matching only.

**Certificate domains considered:** `certificate_update` messages only. CN and SAN entries are lowercased, trimmed, deduped, and wildcard prefixes are stripped (`*.brand.com` → `brand.com`) before matching. If `CT_INGESTION_TLD_FILTER_ENABLED=true`, a cert/domain is considered only when at least one domain TLD is in the per-program union (plus asset-scope apex TLDs); default is disabled, so all TLDs are matched.

**Alert-producing conditions, in order:**
- **dnstwist variation:** after public-suffix stripping, the cert hostname label exactly equals a precomputed dnstwist variation label. Match type is `dnstwist:<fuzzer>` and score is `0.95`. The lookup is TLD-agnostic; `d0main.live` can match a variation generated from `domain.com`.
- **keyword:** any protected prefix/keyword is a lowercase substring of the full cert hostname. Match type is `keyword`, protected value is the keyword, and score is `0.90`.
- **protected similarity:** best similarity between any cert hostname suffix fragment and any protected domain is `>= ct_monitor_program_settings.similarity_threshold` (default `0.75`, clamped `0..1`). Score is max of apex-vs-apex and collapsed-alphanumeric Levenshtein similarity; identical collapsed-but-not-literal names cap at `0.99`.

**Skip / suppression conditions:**
- Non-`certificate_update` messages, messages with no domains, queue drops, or TLD-filter misses never reach typosquat matching.
- Proper subdomains of protected FQDNs are skipped as legitimate (`login.brand.com` when `brand.com` is protected). Asset monitoring still runs before this skip.
- Exact protected FQDNs are skipped (`brand.com` when `brand.com` is protected).
- Duplicate SANs within the same certificate are alerted at most once per domain.
- If no dnstwist match exists and no program match states exist, the SAN is ignored.
- Similarity candidates that cannot reach the threshold by collapsed-length bounds skip full Levenshtein safely (`similarity_skipped` stat; no false negatives).
- Similarity non-matches are not durably logged; they are too high-volume for `ct_monitor_logs`.
- After a match, alert publication is suppressed when `/findings/typosquat/search` already has the exact domain for that program (Redis-cached under `ct_monitor:typosquat_exists:*`); API lookup failures fail open and allow publishing.

## Alert Publishing

- **Typosquat:** NATS `events.typosquat.ct_alert`, priority from match type/score.
- **Asset discovery:** NATS `events.assets.ct_subdomain.discovered` after successful `POST /assets` (parsed as `assets.ct_subdomain.discovered`); triggers program notification handlers and custom event-handler rules.

## HTTP Control API

- `GET /status` — full stats (admin UI); not used for Kubernetes probes
- `GET /health` — lightweight; **liveness and readiness** probes use this path only
- `POST /start`, `POST /stop`, `POST /refresh-domains`, `POST /reload-runtime-settings`

## Development Guidelines

### Performance
- **Ingestion TLD filter is off by default** — expect high CertStream volume and large variation maps; use queue backpressure and adequate memory
- When `CT_INGESTION_TLD_FILTER_ENABLED=true`, frames can be filtered **before** the asyncio queue
- Protected-domain reload builds dnstwist variations + precomputed match state (`PreparedProtected`, keyword automaton) via `asyncio.to_thread`; certificate matching uses `certificate_matcher.match_certificate_sync` off the event loop
- Consumer runs a **fixed pool** of `CT_MATCH_CONCURRENCY` worker tasks draining the queue (not task-per-message), so backpressure is real: queue fills → drops at `CERTSTREAM_QUEUE_DROP_WATERMARK` (default 80%)
- Similarity hot path: rapidfuzz Levenshtein with `score_cutoff` at the per-program threshold, plus `similarity_impossible_by_length_prepared` length gate (safe; no false negatives); per-SAN `PreparedTypo` is built once and reused across programs
- `/status` exposes `offered_per_second`, `processed_per_second`, `drop_rate`, `match_in_flight`, `similarity_skipped`
- Tune `CERTSTREAM_QUEUE_MAXSIZE`, `CT_MATCH_CONCURRENCY`, and ct-monitor CPU (e.g. 4 cores in base Deployment)
- certstream-server load-sheds slow clients; keep ct-monitor queue healthy

### Error handling
- CertStream thread reconnects automatically
- NATS publish retries via publisher

### Testing
- Unit tests: `test_certstream_consumer.py`, `test_certstream_k8s.py` (mock K8s/HTTP, no cluster)
- Monitor `/status` for `total_received` / `processed` when ingestion active

