## Troubleshooting

### No certificates received
- `kubectl get pods -l app=certstream-server`; `curl http://certstream:4000/example.json`
- ct-monitor `/status`: `certstream_url`, `certstream_scale_enabled`, `certstream_replicas_desired`
- `kubectl get deploy certstream-server -n reconhawx` — expect 0/0 when no CT programs, 1/1 when enabled
- At least one program with `ct_monitoring_enabled` or `ct_asset_monitoring_enabled`

### No assets submitted
- `/status`: `any_program_ct_asset_monitoring_enabled`, `programs_asset_enabled` (apex roots per program), `asset_matches`, `assets_submitted`, `asset_dedup_hits`, `post_failures`
- Program needs valid in-scope rules (`scope_domains` or legacy `domain_regex`) — programs without rules or an id are skipped at refresh
- API re-checks scope on ingest; out-of-scope hostnames count as `out_of_scope` in the assets job, not inserts

### No alerts
- Protected domains loaded (`/status` → `protected_domains.total > 0`)
- TLD allowlist covers target domains
- Similarity threshold not too high

### NATS failures
- `publisher.is_connected`, EVENTS stream subjects

